Step 14.1 is complete. All four gates are green: **767 backend tests passed**, **280 vitest passed**, frontend build succeeded, docs drift check OK.

## What I found

The last commit (`7d6a6d54 chore(loop): absorb uncommitted changes before step 14.1`) had already absorbed a partial 14.1 attempt: `media_jobs.py` (1082 lines) plus `test_media_jobs.py` (692 lines). That work covered the service in isolation but was **not wired into anything** — `grep` found zero non-test callers. It also left the suite red (`media_jobs.py` named the `fixture_async` test provider, tripping the zero-touch invariant in `test_provider_extensibility.py`).

## What I did

**Wired both visual domains onto the service.** Storyboard and Animator each carried their own copy of the wait loop — own deadline, own cancel check, own ready/error arithmetic, no progress reporting. Both now delegate to a new shared bridge, `studio/workflows/adapters/media_job.py:153`. The domains differ only in data (manifest path, start callable, failure code), so there is no domain branch in the shared path. This closes D33 (job persistence for *both* visual domains), D31, D34 and D29 for the visual adapters.

**Fixed three defects found by wiring it up:**
- `status_from_scenes` (`jobs.py:229`) counted the `-1` job-level sentinel that `gemini_ws.py:396-398` writes into the per-scene map as a real unit — inflating both `total` and `ready`. Every legacy counter excludes it by hand; the shared helper did not.
- `units_from_legacy_scenes` carried `/output/...` paths straight into the persisted job record, contrary to §31.2. Now normalized to managed relative refs.
- `_request_total` guessed `max(index) + 1`, which over-counts whenever scene indices are sparse — exactly what the adapters' `if scene.get("image_prompt")` filter produces. An explicit `unit_count` now wins.

## Preserved deliberately

Public job IDs stay `project_id`; `storyboard.json` / `grabber_job.json` remain authoritative with `media_job.json` written beside them; the `{total, ready, errors}` port shape is unchanged; `CANCELLED` / `POLL_TIMEOUT` / `STORYBOARD_FAILED` / `ANIMATOR_FAILED` all still surface as before. Animator still omits `scene_statuses` from its port, since those entries carry remote URLs (D38 belongs to 14.3).

## Two adjustments worth recording

1. **Poll cadence moved from 1 s to the frozen 10 s** (`DOMAIN_POLL_INTERVAL_S`). Completion and cancellation are now noticed up to ~11 s later on jobs whose deadlines are 30 and 120 minutes. This follows the frozen §33.3 table rather than the ad-hoc local-file poll.
2. **Staging/promotion is a no-op for this bridge.** The step says the service owns it, but the legacy providers write assets straight into the managed tree while the UI previews them live — introducing staging now would break that preview. Real staging belongs with the provider migrations in 14.2/14.3.

New tests (`tests/test_media_job_bridge.py`, 24 cases) drive the real adapters with scripted legacy stores, parametrized over both domains with identical expectations — so a domain-specific branch would show up as a divergence between parameters rather than needing a source-level grep.

